        <body>
            <div xml:id="d178">

                <pb facs="0445" n="349" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg349"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.419/218</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Houghton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-07-31"><hi rendition="#italic">July 31,
                        1926</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received August 13.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1245</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to my despatch
                    No. 1229 of July 27, 1926,<anchor n="89" xml:id="d178-f1"/> relating to the
                    report of the discussions between British and American officials with regard to
                    liquor smuggling, and to forward herewith the original text of the memorandum
                    signed by General Andrews and Mr. Vansittart, of the Foreign Office.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. A.
                            Sterling</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Counselor of
                        Embassy</hi></closer>



                <xi:include href="d178-a1.xml" xpointer="d178-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
